{{!
    @template mod_playerpuzzle/howtoplay_dialog

    The How to play help during the fight, as a native <dialog> opened from the stage's How to play button. It is moved
    inside the game's container when the game boots, so it also shows in full screen. The title takes the focus when it
    opens, so a screen reader starts from it; the content scrolls and the Close button stays in view.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * title - The dialog's title
    * closelabel - The close button's text
    * All the variables of mod_playerpuzzle/howtoplay_body

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "How to play",
        "closelabel": "Close",
        "goalheading": "The goal",
        "goaltext": "Swap two neighbouring pieces to line up three or more of a kind.",
        "turntext": "You move, then the opponent moves.",
        "piecesheading": "The seven pieces",
        "pieces": [],
        "difficultyheading": "Difficulty",
        "difficultytext": "You choose Easy, Normal or Hard.",
        "difficulties": [],
        "modeheading": "Game mode",
        "modetext": "A Campaign has 1 level of 10 phases.",
        "controlsheading": "Moving the pieces",
        "pointertext": "With a mouse or touch, press a piece and then a neighbour.",
        "keyboardtext": "With the keyboard, use Tab, the arrow keys and Enter.",
        "buttonsheading": "Game buttons",
        "buttons": []
    }
}}
<dialog id="playerpuzzle-howto" class="pp-howto-dialog pp-themed" aria-labelledby="pp-howto-title">
    <h3 id="pp-howto-title" class="pp-howto-title" tabindex="-1">{{title}}</h3>
    {{> mod_playerpuzzle/howtoplay_body }}
    <div class="pp-howto-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="pp-howto-close">{{closelabel}}</button>
    </div>
</dialog>
